      "description": "On Turn 1 with only Polluted Delta on the battlefield and the opponent having just played an Undercity Sewers (tapped), there's no reason not to crack Polluted Delta during the opponent's end step or during combat to get a land untapped. By not activating Polluted Delta at all during Turn 1, the player is delaying their mana development. More importantly, cracking the fetch now would enable having 2 mana available on Turn 2 (the fetched land plus whatever land they play). The player will likely need to crack it on their own turn 2 anyway, but doing it at end of opponent's turn or during this combat step is free - it costs nothing extra and keeps options open. However, since they're going to untap and can crack it on their own turn before playing a land, the actual tempo loss is minimal. The reasoning given ('sacrificing it isn't beneficial at this point') is incorrect - you always want to fetch at the last possible moment before you need the mana, but not fetching at all this turn when you could is a slight missed optimization for information hiding and revolt enabling.",
