      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 119,
      "player": "Haiku ESPN",
      "decision_index": 102,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Discarded Watery Grave instead of a duplicate legendary Gran-Gran. With only 4 lands on board and expensive Archon of Cruelty in hand (8 mana), the extra land drop would help reach higher mana counts. A second Gran-Gran is largely dead due to the legendary rule since one is already on the battlefield.",
      "action_taken": "Discarded Watery Grave and Fatal Push",
      "better_line": "Discard duplicate Gran-Gran and Fatal Push (or second Fatal Push), keeping the land to help eventually cast Archon of Cruelty or have more mana flexibility",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 120,
      "player": "Haiku ESPN",
      "decision_index": 102,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "With only 3 lands (Island, Field of Ruin, Steam Vents) and 8 cards in hand including reactive spells like Counterspell, Force of Negation, and removal, Llama4 Johnny should prioritize using Field of Ruin to destroy one of the opponent's nonbasic lands. This would get them a basic land (fixing mana and ramping to 4 lands), thin their deck, and disrupt the opponent's mana. Casting Consult the Star Charts with only 3 lands means looking at only 3 cards and putting 1 in hand - a mediocre outcome. Additionally, they're stuck on 3 lands and need to develop their mana to cast their spells. Field of Ruin costs 2+T+sacrifice, which they could activate, getting a basic land untapped. This would help them hold up Counterspell or double Fatal Push next turn.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Consult the Star Charts (looking at only 3 cards, keeping 1) using 2 mana, leaving only Field of Ruin untapped.",
      "better_line": "Activate Field of Ruin targeting one of the opponent's nonbasic lands (Watery Grave or Undercity Sewers) to search for a basic land, increasing land count to 3 untapped lands and disrupting opponent's mana. This also enables holding up Counterspell on the opponent's turn.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 121,
      "player": "Llama4 Johnny",
      "decision_index": 104,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Llama4 Johnny is at 9 life facing attackers and has only 3 lands on the battlefield (Island, Field of Ruin, Steam Vents). Their hand is loaded with reactive spells (3x Fatal Push, 2x Sheoldred's Edict, Counterspell, Force of Negation) but critically needs more mana to cast multiple spells per turn. However, looking at the choices - Flooded Strand, Swamp, Sheoldred's Edict - the player already has 3 Fatal Pushes and 2 Sheoldred's Edicts in hand, so another Edict is less needed than a land drop. Flooded Strand is a fetchland that can find Islands or Swamps, which is flexible. But Swamp would be the better pick here since it enters untapped immediately (Flooded Strand costs 1 life to crack when at 9 life, and the player already has blue sources). With the board state showing they need to deploy removal efficiently, getting a Swamp that enters untapped for free is slightly better than a fetchland that costs a life point and requires an additional step. The life total of 9 makes that 1 life relevant against the attacking creatures.",
      "action_taken": "Chose Flooded Strand over Swamp from Consult the Star Charts",
      "better_line": "Choose Swamp - it enters untapped without costing life, providing the black mana needed for Fatal Push and Sheoldred's Edict while preserving the precious life total at 9 life.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 122,
      "player": "Llama4 Johnny",
      "decision_index": 107,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Llama4 Johnny fetched a basic Island when their hand contains 5 black spells (3x Fatal Push, 2x Sheoldred's Edict) and they have ZERO black mana sources on the battlefield. At 8 life with the opponent attacking for 2+ per turn, they desperately need to start removing threats. Fetching Island leaves them completely unable to cast any of their removal spells.",
      "action_taken": "Fetched a basic Island, leaving them with no black mana sources despite a hand full of black removal spells.",
      "better_line": "Fetch Watery Grave (paying 2 life to have it enter untapped) to gain access to black mana, enabling Fatal Push on Psychic Frog or Gran-Gran this turn. Even going to 6 life is worth it to start interacting with the opponent's board.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 125,
      "player": "Llama4 Johnny",
      "decision_index": 112,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Discarded Thoughtseize instead of the redundant second Gran-Gran. With Gran-Gran already on the battlefield (legendary), the second copy is dead weight until the first dies. Thoughtseize could strip a counterspell or removal from the opponent's hand at 6 life, potentially enabling lethal attacks.",
      "action_taken": "Discarded Persist and Thoughtseize",
      "better_line": "Discard Persist and one of the two Gran-Gran copies, keeping Thoughtseize to strip the opponent's answers when they're at 6 life.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 136,
      "player": "Haiku ESPN",
      "decision_index": 115,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Llama4 Johnny fetched Island with Field of Ruin while having ZERO black mana sources on board and a hand full of black spells (3x Fatal Push, 2x Sheoldred's Edict). After this fetch, they have Islands and Steam Vents but cannot cast any of their 5 black removal spells, leaving them unable to interact with the opponent's creatures at 5 life.",
      "action_taken": "Fetched a basic Island, leaving them with no black mana sources.",
      "better_line": "Fetch Watery Grave (paying 2 life to enter untapped, going to 3 life) to gain access to black mana, enabling Fatal Push and Sheoldred's Edict to deal with Psychic Frog and Gran-Gran. Even at 3 life, being able to remove threats is more important than preserving 2 life with no way to interact.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 139,
      "player": "Llama4 Johnny",
      "decision_index": 118,
    },
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Discarding Orcish Bowmasters when facing repeated card draw from Gran-Gran and Psychic Frog seems questionable. Bowmasters is excellent against the opponent's strategy since Gran-Gran draws a card when tapped (triggering Bowmasters) and Psychic Frog draws on combat damage. With 5 lands in play, casting Bowmasters is easy, and it provides both a body to block and punishment for the opponent's card draw engine. One of the three Fatal Pushes or one of the two Sheoldred's Edicts would be more redundant to discard.",
      "action_taken": "Discarded Orcish Bowmasters",
      "better_line": "Discard a third Fatal Push or second Sheoldred's Edict, keeping Orcish Bowmasters as a powerful answer to the opponent's card-draw-heavy gameplan with Gran-Gran and Psychic Frog.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 150,
      "player": "Llama4 Johnny",
      "decision_index": 125,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Discarded Spell Pierce over a duplicate legendary Gran-Gran. There's already a Gran-Gran on the battlefield, making extra copies completely uncastable due to the legend rule. Spell Pierce, while somewhat weakened against an opponent with 5 mana, still has potential utility as a cheap counterspell to protect Psychic Frog from removal. Both could serve as Psychic Frog discard fodder, but Spell Pierce has strictly more utility than a dead legendary duplicate.",
      "action_taken": "Discarded Spell Pierce",
      "better_line": "Discard one of the duplicate Gran-Grans, which cannot be cast due to the legend rule with Gran-Gran already on the battlefield.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 149,
      "player": "Haiku ESPN",
      "decision_index": 124,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Discarded Abhorrent Oculus, which is actually castable at 3 mana (2U + exile 6 from graveyard, which they have 19 cards to work with) and provides a powerful 5/5 flyer with manifest dread value. Meanwhile, they kept three copies of Archon of Cruelty at 8 mana when they only have 3 lands and already have an Archon in the graveyard as a Persist target.",
      "action_taken": "Discarded Abhorrent Oculus",
      "better_line": "Discard one of the three Archon of Cruelty copies. They already have Archon in the graveyard for Persist, and Abhorrent Oculus is actually castable with current mana and provides immediate board impact.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 155,
      "player": "Haiku ESPN",
      "decision_index": 128,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Cling to Dust is quite valuable here - it's a cheap instant that exiles graveyard threats (opponent has Archon of Cruelty, 3x Abhorrent Oculus, reanimation spells in graveyard), can gain 3 life at a precarious 5 life total, and has escape for repeated use. Meanwhile, the hand has redundant removal (2x Fatal Push, 2x Sheoldred's Edict) against only two small creatures.",
      "action_taken": "Discarded Cling to Dust",
      "better_line": "Discard a second copy of Sheoldred's Edict or Fatal Push, keeping Cling to Dust for its graveyard hate, life gain, and mana efficiency against the opponent's reanimation-heavy graveyard.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 162,
      "player": "Llama4 Johnny",
      "decision_index": 136,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Playing Field of Ruin instead of Polluted Delta is suboptimal. Polluted Delta is a fetch land that can find an Island or Swamp, giving mana flexibility and thinning the deck. Field of Ruin requires spending 2 mana plus sacrificing itself to destroy a nonbasic land, which is a tempo-negative play. The opponent has Undercity Sewers and Watery Grave as nonbasic lands, but spending 2 mana to destroy one when you're at 5 life facing creatures on board is not a priority. Playing Polluted Delta first gives you access to 5 mana (4 Islands + Steam Vents) plus the Delta ready to fetch if needed, and you can always play Field of Ruin next turn. Additionally, the reasoning says 'Let's play Flooded Strand' which doesn't match either choice, suggesting confused decision-making.",
      "action_taken": "Played Field of Ruin as the land for turn instead of Polluted Delta.",
      "better_line": "Play Polluted Delta as the land for turn, keeping it available to fetch at instant speed for revolt (enabling Fatal Push to kill 4-mana-value creatures) or to fix mana. Field of Ruin could be played on a later turn.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 163,
      "player": "Llama4 Johnny",
      "decision_index": 139,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Llama4 Johnny has 4 black spells in hand (2x Sheoldred's Edict, 2x Fatal Push) but zero black mana sources on the battlefield. Fetching Island means they still cannot cast any of their removal spells against the opponent's creatures (Psychic Frog and Gran-Gran). At 4 life facing attackers, being unable to interact is likely game-losing.",
      "action_taken": "Fetched Island from library with Polluted Delta",
      "better_line": "Fetch Swamp (enters untapped, no life cost) to gain access to black mana and be able to cast Fatal Push or Sheoldred's Edict to deal with the opponent's threats. Even Watery Grave at 2 life would be better than having no black sources at all.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 165,
      "player": "Llama4 Johnny",
      "decision_index": 141,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Missed lethal on board. Psychic Frog can be pumped to 4/2 by discarding 3 cards, then attack into an empty board for exactly 4 damage (opponent at 4 life). Additionally, casting a second Gran-Gran triggers the legend rule, destroying one of them for no benefit.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Gran-Gran (legendary duplicate) in precombat main instead of going to combat.",
      "better_line": "Go to combat, discard 3 cards to Psychic Frog to pump it to 4/2, attack for lethal damage against the empty board.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 170,
      "player": "Haiku ESPN",
      "decision_index": 144,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Opponent is at 4 life. Psychic Frog can be pumped by discarding cards for +1/+1 counters. Haiku ESPN has multiple uncastable cards in hand (3x Archon of Cruelty at 8 mana with only ~3 lands). Discarding 3 cards to pump Psychic Frog from 1/2 to 4/5 would deal exactly 4 damage = lethal. Instead, Psychic Frog attacked as a 1/2 dealing only 1 damage.",
      "action_taken": "Attacked with Psychic Frog as a 1/2 for only 1 damage, leaving opponent at 3 life.",
      "better_line": "Before or during combat, discard 3 cards (e.g., Archon of Cruelty copies that are uncastable) to Psychic Frog's ability, pumping it to 4/5, then attack for exactly lethal 4 damage.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 175,
      "player": "Haiku ESPN",
      "decision_index": 149,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Psychic Frog is attacking (tapped) and the opponent is at 3 life. Before combat damage, Haiku ESPN could discard 2 cards to put 2 +1/+1 counters on Psychic Frog, making it a 3/4, dealing exactly 3 damage for lethal. They had 7 cards in hand and could easily afford to discard.",
      "action_taken": "Declined to activate Psychic Frog's pump ability during combat, dealing only 1 damage instead of lethal.",
      "better_line": "Discard 2 cards to Psychic Frog's ability to pump it to 3/4 and deal exactly 3 lethal combat damage.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 179,
      "player": "Haiku ESPN",
      "decision_index": 150,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Discarded Polluted Delta (a much-needed 4th land) instead of one of three Archon of Cruelty copies that cost 8 mana and are uncastable for many turns. With only 3 lands in play, the land drop is critical for casting Persist (which can reanimate an Archon from the graveyard) and other cheap spells. There's already an Archon in the graveyard as a reanimation target, making the extra copies in hand redundant.",
      "action_taken": "Discarded Polluted Delta",
      "better_line": "Discard one of the three Archon of Cruelty copies, keeping the land to ensure a 4th land drop and enable casting Persist or other cheap spells to close out the game against an opponent at 3 life.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 183,
      "player": "Haiku ESPN",
      "decision_index": 152,
    },
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Orcish Bowmasters provides unique value in this spot - it's a flash creature that punishes Gran-Gran's draw trigger, creates a blocker (critical at 3 life), and serves as both a threat and removal. The hand already has 4 removal spells (2x Fatal Push, 2x Sheoldred's Edict), making one of those more expendable than Bowmasters.",
      "action_taken": "Discarded Orcish Bowmasters",
      "better_line": "Discard one Sheoldred's Edict, as Fatal Push already handles the cheap creatures on board more efficiently, and Bowmasters provides unique utility as a blocker and Gran-Gran punisher.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 182,
      "player": "Llama4 Johnny",
      "decision_index": 151,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Opponent is at 3 life with no creatures on the battlefield. Psychic Frog (1/2) on the battlefield can be pumped by discarding 2 cards to become 3/4, then attack for exactly lethal 3 damage. Instead, Haiku ESPN is casting Persist before combat, wasting mana and potentially missing the kill if the opponent finds interaction.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Persist in precombat main phase to reanimate a creature from graveyard",
      "better_line": "Go to combat, discard 2 cards to Psychic Frog to pump it to 3/4, attack for 3 damage = lethal against opponent at 3 life",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 184,
      "player": "Haiku ESPN",
